# DUPLICATE-EMISSION BUG, asserted as best the grammar allows: the ending
# paragraph prints TWICE, back to back, in the same response. The story names
# the phrase once, as the argument to `win`, and something emits it a second
# time on top of the ending itself.
#
# There is no assertion that can express "this appears exactly once" — the
# grammar has `contains`, `not contains` and exact match, and no count form —
# so a `contains` here passes identically whether the line prints once or
# twice. An exact match would catch it, but only by pinning the atmospherics
# and the cat line alongside it.
